d/validate]} {:db/id "q-90573" :question/id #uuid "e36fadc1-ee32-54a1-9136-21e4fbf1caad" :question/math-academy-id "q-90573" :question/problem "Is the function $h(x,y,z)={x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}-8{z}^{3}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" :question/worked-solution "A function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}h(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}h(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(tx,ty,tz) & =(tx)^{3}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{3}-8(tz)^{3} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}{x}^{3}y+{t}^{4}x{y}^{3}-8{t}^{3}{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}h(x,y,z)={t}^{n}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}-8{z}^{3})\n$$\n\nand so $h(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90573/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3d1d5f5-b46e-5640-b0b5-5d564a04aafd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection/8c6ccd1ae225dad45608d171d586cdfcf37ae570e6c0ddccbc885e41d57c8d1d" :answer/id #uuid "6b3f8410-10db-5d74-a1e9-63e4a44f3fe2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" :answer/id #uuid "61a13a79-d306-562a-92e7-a321f454fba8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" :answer/id #uuid "cdc49884-faf8-514b-a926-c2b9a302e846" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection/50fb656c2766673a5da9bbda1f8db701420ce6e56dfd3c8053f30e63e3d59bf4" :answer/id #uuid "c8f49e8b-71bf-57f9-a0f2-8ce891d992f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3" :answer/id #uuid "1bf79f29-4f23-5a4b-8f84-40855e80f8c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "30d6d841-7e53-5014-9e4a-8351c523a36e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79577/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" :answer-field/choices ["q-79577/selection/8c6ccd1ae225dad45608d171d586cdfcf37ae570e6c0ddccbc885e41d57c8d1d" "q-79577/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" "q-79577/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" "q-79577/selection/50fb656c2766673a5da9bbda1f8db701420ce6e56dfd3c8053f30e63e3d59bf4" "q-79577/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79577" :question/id #uuid "26800737-1d20-5fc8-93e8-d8bcbcdef142" :question/math-academy-id "q-79577" :question/problem "Is the function $f(x,y,z)=2xyz-{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}z$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}f(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty,tz) & =2(tx)(ty)(tz)-(ty)^{3}+(ty)^{2}(tz) \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}xyz-{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{y}^{2}z \\\\  & ={t}^{3}(2xyz-{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}z) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}f(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{3}f(x,y,z)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y,z)$ is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3d1d5f5-b46e-5640-b0b5-5d564a04aafd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" :answer/id #uuid "f41f2221-c162-5699-9560-0cccb211c546" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection/0d9aab313269fa1aadadef9be2ba9550c31d2a560c87e1e2f42ece634285b9e1" :answer/id #uuid "ec728116-cf65-5473-b63d-21c3e13afe63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3" :answer/id #uuid "24dac729-c4a2-5b85-b9fa-806eb0bcd744" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection/1c67f75b88315fc775beaec39eea156cbb1f4a70016ea4bcecbf9048d885bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "f740ae6a-ed59-5897-bbf6-f3c25555cb9d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" :answer/id #uuid "3551b1b7-6fd6-599a-a7a7-4a245ee8ca5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d343bb85-be51-5ab3-9b47-5fae731c4cf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64179/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" :answer-field/choices ["q-64179/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" "q-64179/selection/0d9aab313269fa1aadadef9be2ba9550c31d2a560c87e1e2f42ece634285b9e1" "q-64179/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3" "q-64179/selection/1c67f75b88315fc775beaec39eea156cbb1f4a70016ea4bcecbf9048d885bb6c" "q-64179/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64179" :question/id #uuid "6ab09b8d-c62f-59d4-a051-b0634322aef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64179" :question/problem "Is the function $g(x,y)=2{x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" :question/worked-solution "A function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we try to simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =2(tx)^{3}+3(ty)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}{x}^{3}+3{t}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}g(x,y)={t}^{n}(2{x}^{3}+3{y}^{2})\n$$\n\nand so $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3d1d5f5-b46e-5640-b0b5-5d564a04aafd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection/8c6ccd1ae225dad45608d171d586cdfcf37ae570e6c0ddccbc885e41d57c8d1d" :answer/id #uuid "69979a22-ac07-5e00-9b34-280361fd14fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" :answer/id #uuid "2b18b304-230c-517c-9f7a-46de58dcbf63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3" :answer/id #uuid "60b8c303-b28a-544d-8531-74de5c8ffc42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" :answer/id #uuid "6ae25217-a2a8-52e7-891f-64221d356281" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection/50fb656c2766673a5da9bbda1f8db701420ce6e56dfd3c8053f30e63e3d59bf4" :answer/id #uuid "85ec20b2-6ad2-5c22-b151-579fa41a5bee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Homogeneous of degree $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb13a5f-fd7f-558d-a248-60b080ad5b40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90572/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" :answer-field/choices ["q-90572/selection/8c6ccd1ae225dad45608d171d586cdfcf37ae570e6c0ddccbc885e41d57c8d1d" "q-90572/selection/8fd97678315481609cae715000504e91032416ff2f323acf778d08f99322c255" "q-90572/selection/1b2ee6753479c464d0e128964ee3b46c2f966ad0c7135b33b3ab53f3d405f8f3" "q-90572/selection/574aa3b3f28517c4977ae180d7d2977b4785aecd90e08dfb924cc09b9127dad9" "q-90572/selection/50fb656c2766673a5da9bbda1f8db701420ce6e56dfd3c8053f30e63e3d59bf4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90572" :question/id #uuid "1622bb44-831b-5f90-acde-f314e5aa270b" :question/math-academy-id "q-90572" :question/problem "Is the function $g(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+5{z}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" :question/worked-solution "A function $g(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}g(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty,tz) & =2(tx)^{2}+(tx)(ty)^{2}+5(tz)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{3}x{y}^{2}+5{t}^{2}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}g(x,y,z)={t}^{n}(2{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+5{z}^{2})\n$$\n\nand so $g(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90572/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3d1d5f5-b46e-5640-b0b5-5d564a04aafd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90572"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64175"] :question/problem "Is the function $f(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}+xy-4{z}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}f(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty,tz) & =3(tx)^{2}+(tx)(ty)-4(tz)^{2} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}xy-4{t}^{2}{z}^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+xy-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}f(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{2}f(x,y,z)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y,z)$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "352460e9-f907-5659-997b-eb743962e763" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "2f671610-4a25-5741-9312-4b208402a02b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7154723b-d115-5d6d-97fe-4f88b36d107c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9f8b9ceb-4d97-5c2e-a469-72cfe2b322c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "82836f60-ac9e-592d-bdfd-d3a976b92dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58899065-cf86-5331-a128-02b0f5cc0fe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79578/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-79578/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-79578/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-79578/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-79578/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-79578/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79578" :question/id #uuid "8c5da278-e488-5961-b0d5-3c97c074b513" :question/math-academy-id "q-79578" :question/problem "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(x)=3xy$\n- $g(x,y)={y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}y$\n- $h(x,y)={x}^{3}-4x{y}^{2}+3{y}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is homogeneous of degree $2.$  It is a polynomial of degree $2,$ with no linear or constant terms.\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $3.$ However, it also contains a term $({y}^{2})$ that is of degree $2.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $3.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7eacaa-2c